<title>USA: INTERVIEW-Owens Corning's pink meets rivals.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW-Owens Corning's pink meets rivals.</headline>
<byline>Gilles Castonguay</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Owens Corning expects insulation prices in the U.S. market to drop over the next year as the company known for its pink home insulation defends its market share against competitors, a senior official said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are seeing some price competition and are expecting it to get worse before it gets better,&quot; the company's chief financial officer, David Devonshire, told Reuters.</p>
